# Answer-key firewall for the BLACK-BOX image. Not generated - this file is yours, edit it directly.
#
# The firewall for a black-box session. What must never enter the image:
#   * the shipped sample test suite - it would survive as a fallback and inflate an empty submission
#   * _design/ - the reference test suite used for calibration, which is the answer key here
#
# Note the reference *implementation* IS baked in on purpose: Stryker mutates it. That is why a black-box
# image is even more sensitive than a white-box one and must stay in the private registry.

**/bin/
**/obj/
.idea/
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
**/TestResults/
**/StrykerOutput/
.git/
.github/

# Design-team-only: reference suite, calibration notes, model solutions.
_design/**

# The competitor supplies this at run time. Keep the csproj so restore resolves and swap_dir has a target.
Checkout.Rules.UnitTests/**
!Checkout.Rules.UnitTests/Checkout.Rules.UnitTests.csproj

# The exclusion above is root-anchored, so it does not cover these copies of a UnitTests folder. Neither is
# something the judge runs: competitor-start/ is what gets handed out, submissions/ are samples used from the
# host by judge-run.sh.
competitor-start/**
submissions/**
